WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.960
Which character from the creepy "Werewolf&nbsp;
By Night" special could be gunning for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:08.220
Marvel's most famous vampire hunter? Signs&nbsp;
seem to be pointing to one in particular.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:13.320
Marvel Studios cracked its monster-verse wide open&nbsp;
with the frightening holiday treat "Werewolf by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.520
Night." The black-and-white splatter fest&nbsp;
pays homage to cinema's earliest monsters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.560
and sets the Marvel Cinematic Universe up for&nbsp;
more thrilling bloodshed. The Disney+ original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.400
series "Moon Knight" was definitely a&nbsp;
first step in this spooky direction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.940
leaving room for more iterations&nbsp;
of creature features featuring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:35.580
characters including Ghost Rider, Deathlok,&nbsp;
and perhaps even Marvel's version of Dracula.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:40.860
Marvel Studios has definitely dipped its toe into&nbsp;
some more horror-styled content recently. It even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.480
recruited veteran horror director Sam Raimi,&nbsp;
who brought some small hints of horror to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.820
Sony "Spider-Man" movies in the early 2000s, for&nbsp;
Wanda's terrifying massacre in "Doctor Strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.800
in the Multiverse of Madness." These elements&nbsp;
lay the crucial foundation for Marvel's more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:01.500
horrific adventures and prepare audiences young&nbsp;
and old for more nightmare-inducing moments.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.180
"Who said they had to be living?"

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:08.820
The studio's Phase 4 has included a number of&nbsp;
different genre experiments. The company's ability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:14.160
to adapt to different styles is a promising sign&nbsp;
that it is hungry for fresh and exciting tales,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.940
and it's an excellent time to speculate&nbsp;
where the universe could be headed next.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:22.500
Before Marvel was the cinematic juggernaut&nbsp;
it is today, it did see some success in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.660
the horror realm with the Blade movie trilogy&nbsp;
starring Wesley Snipes as the stylish vampire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:32.940
hunter. Marvel worked with New Line Cinema&nbsp;
on the films, starting with 1998's "Blade."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:38.340
But by the time "Blade: Trinity" came around in&nbsp;
2004, it seemed the series had run its course.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:43.500
Marvel also teamed with Sony to bring one of&nbsp;
its 1970s comic book monsters to the screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:49.680
with 2007's "Ghost Rider" starring Nicolas Cage.&nbsp;
Despite doing reasonably well at the box office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:55.860
it was a dud with critics, with a Rotten&nbsp;
Tomatoes score of 27%. The "Ghost Rider" sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.820
2012's "Spirit of Vengeance," was met&nbsp;
with even worse reception from critics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:05.280
Its Rotten Tomatoes score was 18%. It also&nbsp;
did considerably worse at the box office.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:10.260
This understandably left Marvel Studios&nbsp;
hesitant to return to the flaming-headed biker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:14.760
or to fully embrace horror. An iteration&nbsp;
of Ghost Rider did show up in Marvel's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:17.880
"Agents of SHIELD" television&nbsp;
series to set up his own show.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.740
But following Disney's acquisition&nbsp;
of Fox, his spin-off show was axed.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:27.360
Luckily, that wasn't Marvel's last try at&nbsp;
bringing the horror comics of the 1970s to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:32.040
life on screen. "Werewolf by Night" and "Moon&nbsp;
Knight" have inspired confidence in Marvel's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:36.780
diehard horror fans. The werewolf slasher&nbsp;
even introduced the odd-looking Man-Thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:40.440
paving the way for other scary&nbsp;
characters, including the new Blade.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.820
"Call him by his name."

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:42.480
"Which is?"

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:45.360
"Ted. He's called Ted."

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:49.980
Viewers' first encounter with the MCU's&nbsp;
new version of Blade came at the end of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:54.900
"Eternals." In a post-credits scene, Dane Whitman&nbsp;
is seen inheriting his family's precious and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.900 --> 00:03:00.120
deadly sword: the Ebony Blade. This also indicates&nbsp;
to comic book fans that Whitman will become the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:05.040
Avenger Black Knight. When Whitman picks up the&nbsp;
sword, an instantly recognizable voice cautions,

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:07.740
"Sure you're ready for that, Mr. Whitman?"

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:13.980
The dark sword carries unspeakable consequences,&nbsp;
Mahershala Ali's Blade forewarns. While the Ebony&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:19.620
Blade possesses extraordinary power, it also&nbsp;
drives the user mad over time, causing them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:24.000
commit heinous acts. Blade's warning suggests&nbsp;
he may team up with the Black Knight in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.220
upcoming solo film, which could even feature&nbsp;
a formidable foe seen in "Werewolf by Night."

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:34.080
Elsa Bloodstone made a fiery entrance as&nbsp;
the unapologetic and fearless daughter of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.860
monster-hunter Ulysses Bloodstone.&nbsp;
She unflinchingly survived both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:42.120
the Bloodstone hunt and her encounters&nbsp;
with Man-Thing and the Werewolf himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:47.220
Jack Russell. Her capable display of skill&nbsp;
is even more exciting after she obtains the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:51.900
Bloodstone and her powers, becoming one&nbsp;
of the MCU's deadliest vampire hunters.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.800
While Blade and Elsa may share some&nbsp;
similar goals, Blade's status as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:59.820
daywalker could set up a potential clash&nbsp;
between the two slayers. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:03.780
if they do meet, it's likely they'll have&nbsp;
to team up to take on a bigger threat.

